# --- COMMIT MESSAGE FORMAT ---
# <type>(<scope>): <short summary in present tense>
#
# Allowed Types:
#   feat     - A new feature or user-visible enhancement
#   fix      - A bug fix
#   docs     - Documentation changes only
#   style    - Code style changes (formatting, missing semi-colons, whitespace, etc.)
#   refactor - Code changes that neither fix a bug nor add a feature
#   perf     - Code changes that improve performance
#   test     - Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
#   build    - Changes affecting build system, Gradle, dependencies, compile settings
#   ci       - Changes to CI/CD workflows, Mergeable rules, GitHub Actions
#   chore    - Maintenance tasks, repository housekeeping, minor updates
#   revert   - Reverts a previous commit
#
# Scopes (optional, but recommended):
#   ui         - Compose views, screens, preview wrappers, theme, components
#   data       - Repositories, database (Room), DataStore, file handlers
#   storage    - Local, SMB, or WebDAV file system handlers, FileStreamProvider
#   navigation - Navigation routes, backstack management, drawer/rail
#   security   - Tink encryption, KeyStore, credentials
#   discovery  - Network server discovery (NSD, NetBIOS)
#   deps       - Dependency updates or configuration
#   ci         - Workflows, Mergeable, build configuration
#
# Guidelines for Summary:
#   - Capitalize the first letter or keep lowercase consistently
#   - Use imperative, present tense ("add" not "added", "change" not "changed")
#   - Do NOT end summary with a period
#   - Keep total length under 72 characters
#
# Body (Required):
#   Explain the motivation, context, and what was changed.
#   Use one or more non-comment lines below the subject.
#
# Closes: #<issue number>
